# Mewtual Combined Licence Terms 1.0

These terms consist of both Part I and Part II below. The permissions in Part II are offered
only together with Part I. To receive any licence for the software, you must accept and comply
with both parts as strict obligations and conditions of all your licences. If their terms
conflict, the term granting less permission controls.

Part II reproduces the PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0 verbatim. Part I adds conditions
specific to Mewtual without modifying that standard text.

## Part I: Mewtual No-AI and Source-Disclosure Terms

### No artificial-intelligence use

You may not use the software, a covered work, or any part of either, directly or indirectly:

1. to train, pre-train, fine-tune, align, distil, validate, benchmark, evaluate, test, improve,
   or develop an artificial-intelligence system;
2. to create, curate, label, filter, validate, or supply a dataset intended for use by an
   artificial-intelligence system;
3. as input to an artificial-intelligence system for code generation, code completion,
   translation, summarisation, analysis, retrieval-augmented generation, or a substantially
   similar purpose; or
4. in, with, or as part of a product, service, project, or covered work that implements,
   provides, enables, or is intended to develop or operate an artificial-intelligence system.

Conventional compilation, static analysis, security scanning, code search, indexing, and code
navigation are allowed when their results are not used to train, evaluate, improve, or operate
an artificial-intelligence system.

### Source disclosure and same terms

If you distribute or make a covered work available to anyone, you must, at no charge:

1. provide every recipient with its complete corresponding source at the same time and through
   the same medium, or provide a clear, durable written offer and network location from which
   the recipient can obtain that source for as long as the covered work is available;
2. license the complete corresponding source under these complete combined terms, without
   additional terms that restrict exercise of the permissions they grant; and
3. preserve all copyright, attribution, licensing, and required notices supplied with the
   software.

Third-party components remain governed solely by their own licence terms. The same-terms
requirement in condition 2 above reaches only those parts of the complete corresponding source
that are not third-party components, and nothing in these terms requires or permits you to place
a restriction on a third-party component that its own licence forbids. Where a third-party
licence requires you to pass its text, notices, or source offer on to your recipients, doing so
satisfies these terms rather than conflicting with them.

If you modify a covered work and allow anyone other than you to interact with its functionality
over a computer network, you must give every such user a prominent and readily accessible way
to obtain the complete corresponding source under the same conditions.

You may distribute a covered work only in forms that permit recipients to inspect, build,
modify, and redistribute its complete corresponding source under these terms. You may not use
technical measures or contractual terms to prevent those activities where these terms permit
them.

### Definitions for Part I

**Artificial-intelligence system** means any machine-learning, statistical-learning,
generative, foundation, language, vision, audio, multimodal, neural-network, automated
decision-making, or automated code-generation model, system, or service, regardless of the
technique or description used.

**Covered work** means the software and any modified, adapted, translated, derivative,
combined, or linked work containing or using any copyrightable part of the software. Mere
aggregation of an independent work on the same storage or distribution medium does not make
that independent work a covered work.

**Complete corresponding source** means all source code for a covered work, including the
source code of components that together form a single program with it, plus scripts, interface
definitions, configuration, and other material needed to build, install, run, test, and modify
that work. It does not include general-purpose tools or operating-system components normally
distributed independently of the covered work.

**Software** and **licensor** have the meanings given in Part II. Software does not include
third-party components that identify and remain governed by their own licence terms.

### Violations, fair use, and liability

The Part II sections titled **Violations**, **Fair Use**, and **No Liability** apply equally to
Part I.

These combined terms are source-available, noncommercial licensing and are not an Open Source
Initiative approved open-source licence.

